From 8ef79f960f5a824bee3c7268131d565ee7a90c2d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pierre-Yves MORDRET <pierre-yves.mordret@foss.st.com>
Date: Tue, 26 Nov 2024 17:21:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mfd: stm32-lptimer: use raw_spinlock

In CONFIG_PREEMPT_RT and by enabling Prove Locking Flags,
errors are shown as:
[ 20.723562] rt_spin_lock+0x54/0x114
[ 20.723575] regmap_lock_spinlock+0x18/0x2c
[ 20.723589] regmap_write+0x3c/0x78
[ 20.723598] stm32_clkevent_lp_shutdown+0x24/0x58

It's caused by LPTIMER clkevent driver (used by default on MP25 boards),
that registers the interrupt with IRQF_TIMER flag. As consequence, the
interrupt can't be run from thread context, but uses HW interrupt context
handler, when sleeping isn't possible (RT spin_lock may sleep).
For this case, there's no choice but to use raw_spinlock.
Choice is done no to change current behavior when CONFIG_PREEMPT_RT is
unused.

Change-Id: Id3632785a777b71e1bf58da451e15d29fd433bba
Signed-off-by: Pierre-Yves MORDRET <pierre-yves.mordret@foss.st.com>
Signed-off-by: Fabrice Gasnier <fabrice.gasnier@foss.st.com>
---
 drivers/mfd/stm32-lptimer.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/mfd/stm32-lptimer.c
+++ b/drivers/mfd/stm32-lptimer.c
@@ -20,6 +20,8 @@ static const struct regmap_config stm32_
 	.val_bits = 32,
 	.reg_stride = sizeof(u32),
 	.max_register = STM32_LPTIM_MAX_REGISTER,
+	.fast_io = true,
+	.use_raw_spinlock = IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_PREEMPT_RT) ? true : false,
 };
 
 static int stm32_lptimer_detect_encoder(struct stm32_lptimer *ddata)
